agent-ops task task-a5126dda-5784-41eb-9282-8ba1374cca02: Slim DEBUG to a red-to-green task
intent: Agreed grill 2026-10-22 (Q1-Q9): DEBUG becomes a normal task plus a required baseline-red/candidate-green behavioral criterion. Remove hypothesis, strategy, rounds, budget/extend/grant, native control words, DEBUG Stop gate, checkpoint/resume, prompt-hook intake and transcript parsing; task debug returns TASK_DEBUG_REMOVED; origin/escape become advisory; legacy state/config load and are ignored. Task B (evidence/base/checkIds/surface-at-verify) follows separately.
criteria:
- removed-ceremony: task debug with any action returns TASK_DEBUG_REMOVED; Claude/Codex UserPromptSubmit hooks never create a DEBUG task or inject DEBUG intake text; Stop hooks (Claude, Codex, agy) never block or require a checkpoint because of a DEBUG task; verify never refuses with TASK_DEBUG_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED.
- red-check-required: task create --debug without a behavioral criterion carrying redCheckIds fails with TASK_DEBUG_RED_CHECK_REQUIRED and without a surface fails like any task; a --debug task with one completes under normal completion rules (proven acceptance coverage plus review) with no hypothesis, origin or budget.
- legacy-compat: A task state written by 0.10.x containing task.debug, record.debug (hypotheses, budget, grants, checkpoint), originRequired and an attestation with debugProofs loads and the task can complete under normal rules; a config with features.debug {enabled,budgetMs,maxRounds} validates and is ignored.
- origin-advisory: A --debug task with no declared origin completes (no ESCAPE_ORIGIN_MISSING); task revise --escape-of on a --debug task records the origin and writes the escape ledger like a normal task.
- docs-install: init/update stop writing features.debug and resolve no task-debug capability; managed CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md, CLI help, task-debug guides and spec (en and zh-TW) describe the slim DEBUG flow without budgets or control words; npm test passes.
