agent-ops task task-5947cda1-cf74-4140-bd5c-f6510d3bd4f8: Stop evidence going stale on metadata changes
intent: Agreed grill 2026-10-22 Q3-Q5 (Task B of the DEBUG slim-down): bind only red checks, default --base, task revise --baseline, verify evidence bound to an execution hash so surface/origin/goal revises keep it, .agent-ops-escapes-only commits keep the base-mode fingerprint, and verify reports the surface gate as advisory.
criteria:
- red-only-checkids: A behavioral binding listing only its red checkIds proves red-to-green when the runner also emits other passing checks; a listed check that is missing stays UNKNOWN missing-check; an unlisted check failing on the candidate keeps the candidate from passing.
- default-base: With no --base and a clean tree, verify and review in a session worktree use its merge-base with the target branch, and in the main checkout the task creation commit when it is an ancestor of HEAD; a dirty tree keeps worktree mode; task revise --baseline <commit> moves every typed criterion baseline and clears verification evidence.
- metadata-keeps-evidence: A revise that changes only surface or origin keeps PASS verification evidence usable for completion while requiring a fresh review; a revise that changes criteria clears it; evidence carrying the pre-0.11 full contract hash still matches an unchanged contract.
- ledger-fingerprint: In base mode a commit that touches only .agent-ops-escapes/** leaves the source fingerprint unchanged, while a commit touching any other path changes it.
- surface-at-verify: verify prints the surface gate result (code and unclassified paths) as advisory output without changing its status or envelope code; spec (en and zh-TW) and CHANGELOG describe all Task B behavior; npm test passes.
